WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.320
This is Sealbook, on a fictional case built from open media.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.120
Five files arrive about one street: a photo, a video, a voice note, and two posts.

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:21.560
Each one is fingerprinted and read. Nothing it proposes is fact yet.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:27.820
On the photo, every line and label is boxed where it is seen.

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:35.120
Then the first pass of your method, with a title in two languages.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.740
On the video, each line rests on the second it shows.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.860
Everything waiting on you, in one list.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:54.040
Two posts report one event. You say which Aleppo they mean.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.160
You see every row before you sign, with one passkey.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.020
And the case has an incident, with its place and its day.

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.300
You judge. Sealbook does the first pass.
